                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Not sure about why commenting out `vim.notify` makes it work, but `vim.b.term_title` is already automatically set (at least on Neovim 0.12.3).\r\n\r\nSo instead of autocommand for setting `vim.b.term_title`, it can be for just redrawing tabline:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('TermRequest', {\r\n  desc = 'Redraw when OSC0 or OSC2 is issued (set title)',\r\n  callback = function(args)\r\n    local title = args.data.sequence:match('^\\27%][02];(.*)$')\r\n    if title ~= nil then vim.cmd.redrawtabline() end\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Not sure about why commenting out <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.notify</code> makes it work, but <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.term_title</code> is already automatically set (at least on Neovim 0.12.3).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So instead of autocommand for setting <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.term_title</code>, it can be for just redrawing tabline:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('TermRequest', {\n  desc = 'Redraw when OSC0 or OSC2 is issued (set title)',\n  callback = function(args)\n    local title = args.data.sequence:match('^\\27%][02];(.*)$')\n    if title ~= nil then vim.cmd.redrawtabline() end\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>TermRequest<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Redraw when OSC0 or OSC2 is issued (set title)<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">title</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">data</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">sequence</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">match</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\27</span>%][02];(.*)$<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">title</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">cmd</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">redrawtabline</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Not sure about why commenting out vim.notify makes it work, but vim.b.term_title is already automatically set (at least on Neovim 0.12.3).\nSo instead of autocommand for setting vim.b.term_title, it can be for just redrawing tabline:\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('TermRequest', {\n  desc = 'Redraw when OSC0 or OSC2 is issued (set title)',\n  callback = function(args)\n    local title = args.data.sequence:match('^\\27%][02];(.*)$')\n    if title ~= nil then vim.cmd.redrawtabline() end\n  end,\n})",
